'' A FIXED array's LBOUND and UBOUND fold at compile time. The comment on the runtime
'' path said so and the code returned false instead, so every one of them declined --
'' and with it the whole statement it was in. Measured: fbc emits the four constants
'' 2, 9, 0 and 3 for 'dim b_( 2 to 9, 0 to 3 )'. The dimension is ONE-BASED in the
'' source and zero-based in the layout, and an unknown bound declines rather than
'' folding to whatever the table happens to hold.
''
'' 'type<T>( )' WITH NO ARGUMENTS is the default constructor on a temporary --
'' '_ZN1CC1Ev( &TMP$2$0 )' and then a read out of TMP -- and fbc REJECTS the empty
'' form over a type that has no constructor, so there is no zeroing case beside it.
'' The field-list walk had nothing to iterate and returned as though it had done the
'' work, so the temporary was never constructed.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/fixed-bounds.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/fixed-bounds.out
